{"packet_id":"3df28c31ad2b7f92","dimensions":{"problem_framing":{"status":"scored","score":2,"event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1 separates the objective (whether evidence justifies investment) from the suggested solution. It lists real alternatives, including a route-to-market change and a different customer group, and states constraints. It does not correct the question's premise: the dossier returned in A2-A8 shows Hach/ETS already sells consumer pool and spa strips (AquaChek), so 'beyond its current B2B offerings' is not accurate. That keeps it from rung 3."},"causal_mechanism":{"status":"scored","score":2,"event_ids":["A9"],"reason":"T1 (A9) states who changes behaviour (DIY homeowners), why (water-safety awareness, brand trust) and how value is captured (premium kits). The value-capture link is asserted, not traced: it assumes B2B distribution and consumer brand trust carry over to consumers. No source supports that, so it falls short of a full chain to captured value."},"distinct_theories":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"T2 (A10) is a near-verbatim template of T1 (A9) with 'health' swapped for 'regulatory compliance'. Both imply the same product (premium test kit), the same customers (homeowners and small property owners) and the same channel. They are closer to rewordings than to rivals implying different products, customers or channels."},"assumptions_predictions":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"Assumptions are listed. The predictions are vague and conflate stated interest with demand: 'if a survey shows a majority are interested ... the test will generate sufficient demand'. They are also partly circular, and the correlation predictions are not specified well enough that failure would clearly endanger either theory."},"evidence_judgement":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A11","A12","A13","A14"],"reason":"A11 correctly labels hach-distribution-consumers as a company assertion and notes some limits. However, it scores as 'supports' T1 a passage about utility distribution-system field testing; that passage does not concern home buyers. A14 misclassifies hach-pfas-kit-volume, a verified_observation reporting a company estimate, as an 'independent_study'. It also treats 'Cassou estimated' future sales as support for T2 while admitting the source shows nothing about compliance motivation. A14 does not note that buyer type, date and place are unknown. The most relevant source, hach-wi-reasons, was retrieved in A13 but never assessed."},"seeking_challenge":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A13"],"reason":"A13 runs one search against T1 and retrieves hach-wi-reasons. That source reports well owners not testing because water seems safe and not knowing what to test for, which bears directly on T1's demand premise. Its content is never reported or weighed. No challenge search is made against T2."},"experiment_design":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A15"],"reason":"The episode stopped at the turn limit (A15) before any test was proposed or declined."},"revision":{"status":"not_applicable","score":null,"event_ids":[],"reason":"Revision is excluded from packet.applicable_dimensions, and no update was scheduled."},"recommendation":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A15"],"reason":"A15: the investigation stopped before a recommendation. This contributes zero to the all-case composite."}},"red_flags":[{"kind":"incomplete","event_ids":["A15"],"reason":"The episode ended at the turn limit with no recommendation."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A11"],"reason":"A utility distribution-system passage about field testing before water reaches consumers is scored as supporting consumer demand for home testing. The source does not establish that."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A14"],"reason":"A management sales estimate, mislabelled as an independent study and with unknown buyer type, is scored as supporting a compliance-driven homeowner theory. The assessment itself admits the source does not show compliance motivation."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"Hypotheses are stated as fact without any source: Hach as a 'well-known' trusted consumer brand, 'regulatory bodies increasingly require' homeowner testing, and B2B distribution being repurposable."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A13"],"reason":"Contrary evidence (hach-wi-reasons) was retrieved in the challenge search and then silently ignored."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A1","A2","A3"],"reason":"The framing missed Hach/ETS's existing consumer pool and spa business (AquaChek), although it appeared repeatedly in the search results."}],"suitable_for_training":false,"screen_reason":"The trajectory is rejected. The episode is incomplete, with no experiment design or recommendation (A15). It also contains material unsupported inferences: utility field-testing text is used as evidence of consumer demand (A11), a company sales estimate is misclassified and used as support for compliance motivation (A14), and retrieved contrary evidence is ignored (A13)."}
